      "content": "that's a pretty strong stance. but i mean, even if we want better policy, can we actually stop the tech from advancing? like, if one country tries to slow down automation through heavy regulation, wouldn't they just fall behind other countries that are racing to develop it? doesn't that make the technological progress itself pretty much inevitable, no matter what the policy is?",
